    "answer": {
      "short": "$(-1+2\\sqrt3\\cos t,4+2\\sqrt3\\sin t)$, $t\\in\\mathbb R$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(x+1)^2+(y-4)^2&=1+16-5\\\\(x+1)^2+(y-4)^2&=12\\end{align*}$$\nThe centre is $(-1,4)$ and the radius is $\\sqrt{12}=2\\sqrt3$.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=-1+2\\sqrt3\\cos t\\\\y&=4+2\\sqrt3\\sin t\\end{align*}$$\nA suitable domain is $t\\in\\mathbb R$.",
